reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124552","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124552.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124552.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\nTo aid in the inetgration of `clangd-tidy` checks across the repository, this narrows the CI exclusions significantly by utilizing macro wrappers. `clangd-tidy` won't attempt to parse sections that aren't in a defined scope, so these wrappers will effectively make those files no-op.\n\n## Additional information\n\nExcludes the `platform/` folders still, as the scope would've easily doubled with their inclusion. There's also arguments to be made for applying wrappers to `modules`/`editor` as well, but it's a reasonable assumption that whatever `compile_commands.json` is used was built with maximal modules as an editor, so their scope is somewhat implicit.\n\nHaving said that: all of the above could be considered for followup PRs if the scope is deemed reasonable.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124552/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}